<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    NEW 22/09/2026, REVISED 23/09/2026 (Yann: "Pour la partie icône, il faut que ça soit exactement
    la même chose que la vue icône du widget 4x1 : 5 icônes, titres, icône cloche ou sport sur la
    gauche. La difference est seulement que la dernière notif n'apparaît pas car est dans vue
    texte") — a SECOND, 4x2 widget (NowBarWidgetProviderCompact), same lock-screen-friendly
    transparent background as widget_now_bar.xml, TWO stacked rows:

    - ROW 1 (top): a BYTE-FOR-BYTE COPY of widget_now_bar.xml's own widget_sofascore_content and
      widget_all_notifs_content blocks below (same ids — see that file's class doc for the full
      per-tile reasoning, unchanged here) plus the SAME left-column icon convention (football
      pitch for Sport, bell for Toutes notifs — just a differently-id'd ImageView,
      widget_compact_row1_icon, since widget_app_icon is already row 2's) and the SAME right
      toggle (widget_view_toggle_right, same id, same icons/PendingIntent as widget_now_bar's
      own) — so NowBarWidgetProvider.applySofascoreMatches/applyAllNotifs/applySofascoreIcon/
      applyAllNotifsIcon/applyRightToggle render this row exactly as they render the main widget's
      own Sport/Toutes-notifs view, unmodified (see NowBarWidgetProviderCompact.applyIconsRow).
      The ONE difference: whichever entry is currently "Dernière notif" (row 2's own content) is
      filtered out of the list BEFORE it's handed to those same functions — "la dernière notif
      n'apparaît pas car est dans vue texte" — so a slot that would show it is simply GONE instead
      (never re-numbered), same as when there are fewer than 5 matches/notifs to begin with.

    - ROW 2 (bottom): "Dernière notif" — a byte-for-byte copy of widget_now_bar.xml's left column
      (widget_app_icon/widget_view_toggle) + widget_latest_content block, SAME ids, so
      NowBarWidgetProvider.applyLatestContent/renderLatestFormat/applyPeekLeftColumn (and the
      "peek" mechanism they're already part of — WidgetPeekPrefs, the 15s auto-close alarm) render
      this row exactly as-is — tapping a row-1 tile opens a "peek" (the SAME ACTION_OPEN_PEEK
      broadcast widget_now_bar's own tiles use, just a different request-code range — see
      NowBarWidgetProviderCompact.PEEK_REQUEST_CODE_*) that shows full-format here instead of the
      true latest notification, and the SAME 15s alarm closes it automatically, falling back to
      "Dernière notif" again. widget_view_toggle (the small arrows glyph) only ever appears here
      while peeking, bound to "close the peek" exactly like widget_now_bar's own — there's no
      separate LATEST-away "grid" view in THIS widget to switch to otherwise (row 1 covers that
      permanently), so it's GONE the rest of the time.
-->
